# DEV-45, SP-22 (b): a member's own Remove and the instance's Remove of the same call leaf, in both
# orders, followed by another member's commit. OpenMLS keeps only the later of two Removes of one
# leaf, so before dilla-media task 9 the first order ended in 422 outstanding_proposals until the
# instance's Remove voided at the call TTL. Now carol's own Remove voids the instance's (order 1),
# and the instance drops its device-addressed Remove of dave's leaf because dave's own stands
# (order 2): alice's commit is accepted both times, bob's client accepts it (a referenced member
# Remove is measured against its proposer), and both are out.
#
# "Out" is checked through the instance, not by the leaver sending: a client holding its own
# pending Remove cannot create an application message (OpenMLS refuses with PendingProposal). A
# repeated kick of a device that still held a leaf would leave a Remove outstanding — re-driven
# from the old epoch or freshly proposed — and the send after it would answer 425; a kick of a
# device that is gone is dropped, and the send goes through.
instance dilla
client alice
client bob
client carol
client dave
group call kind=call target=e2e2e2e2e2e2e2e2e2e2e2e2e2e2e2e2 community=none creator=alice
join bob call via=external
sync alice
join carol call via=external
sync alice
sync bob
join dave call via=external
sync alice
sync bob
sync carol
kick alice carol
leave carol call
commit alice call
sync bob
sync dave
kick alice carol
send alice call carol is out after order one
expect_decrypts bob call carol is out after order one
leave dave call
kick alice dave
commit alice call
sync bob
kick alice dave
send alice call carol and dave are out
expect_decrypts bob call carol and dave are out
